# cursor install

**Read [`memory/cursor-install.md`](../memory/cursor-install.md) before going further.** This rule exists to
fire on the topic and send you there; the knowledge itself lives in one place, not two.

**Why it is worth the read:** Cursor marketplace sparse-checkout only keeps `/.cursor-plugin/` and `/.claude-plugin/`. Moving the plugin back to the repo root looks cleaner and silently empties every Cursor install.

## Before you touch anything

- The shippable tree is `.cursor-plugin/ultimate-workflow/`. Marketplace `source` fields must point there, not at github-of-self root.
- `mirrors.test.js` sparse-cone and ZIP membership checks are the control — a green suite without them is not evidence the install works.
- Root `AGENTS.md` is dogfood for this repo; it is not what Cursor loads from a plugin install.

---

*This rule is Cursor's retrieval mechanism for `memory/`. On Claude Code the same
topical is reached through the Read-when cue in `memory.md`. Cursor does not act on
that pointer, so without this rule the topicals were unreachable here -- the rule is
the selector, the topical is the content, and neither duplicates the other.*
